{"hash":"ed310c31515e21e8","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":71.721,"said":"Before you go to Somnath, greet the one who guards the way. In the old Prabhasa texts, the Ganesha of this sacred land is Shri Kapardi Vinayak, and the Skanda Purana gives him a whole chapter. Its story is a gentle warning. The gods once complained that Somnath’s grace was too easy: anyone at all could reach heaven just by coming here. So the Goddess shaped Ganesha and sent him to guard this land, setting obstacles before those who came without a true heart. That is why the text asks every pilgrim to bow to Kapardin first, ‘for freedom from obstacles in the course of the pilgrimage’, and promises that remembering him brings the merit of every tirtha and every sacrifice. In Somnath today his shrine is honoured with Siddhi and Buddhi beside him, and local tradition links it with Adi Shankaracharya. So fold your hands here, as pilgrims have done for centuries, and ask him to clear your path. Then go on to the Lord, with nothing left in your way.\n\nDid you know? In the Skanda Purana, the Goddess creates Kapardi Vinayak because Somnath’s grace had become too easy to win.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":956},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":972,"end":1081}],"words":[[0.098,0.361,0,6],[0.471,0.096,7,10],[0.579,0.168,11,13],[0.759,0.12,14,16],[0.891,0.637,17,24],[1.745,0.337,26,31],[2.093,0.12,32,35],[2.225,0.264,36,39],[2.502,0.132,40,43],[2.646,0.312,44,50],[2.971,0.108,51,54],[3.091,0.288,55,58],[4.291,0.12,60,62],[4.423,0.12,63,66],[4.555,0.252,67,70],[4.82,0.541,71,79],[5.373,0.553,80,85],[6.154,0.108,87,90],[6.274,0.517,91,98],[6.803,0.168,99,101],[6.983,0.192,102,106],[7.188,0.445,107,113],[7.644,0.397,114,118],[8.053,0.132,119,121],[8.197,0.264,122,126],[8.474,0.517,127,134],[9.002,0.529,135,142],[9.748,0.192,144,147],[9.952,0.084,148,151],[10.048,0.349,152,158],[10.409,0.445,159,165],[10.865,0.325,166,171],[11.202,0.18,172,175],[11.394,0.06,176,177],[11.466,0.